# The story, through the real keys (docs/STORY.md, owner 2026-09-17): nothing
# speaks because the player walked onto a tile. A line is said because they
# pressed a key standing in front of somebody, or in front of a thing that has
# something written on it.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/story.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --folk=6 --put=sign
#
# (--folk rings villagers round the player — one is a keeper, the trade the first
# conversation is written for — and --put stands one of the machines' own notices
# where it can be walked to. Where notices and people really stand is worldgen's
# business and the landmarks package's, not this tour's.)
#
# The conversation comes first on purpose: `use` answers whatever is NEAREST and
# in front, so a tour that read the notice first would press the key again with
# the notice still at its boot and read it twice.
coast calm
wait 0.6

# --- somebody to talk to --------------------------------------------------------------
# A villager walks their own round: if they have stepped out of reach by the time
# the key is pressed, walk them down again rather than failing the tour on it.
try 4
  walkto folk 6
  press use
  await talking 3
end
wait 0.4
shot 01-a-keeper-with-something-to-say with talking,folk

# --- what the player says is theirs, and it is remembered -------------------------------
# Down to the third reply and take it: saying nothing is always on the list, and
# in this arc it is never the cowardly one.
tap move_down
tap move_down
wait 0.3
shot 02-what-you-may-say with talking,folk
press use
wait 0.5
shot 03-said-nothing with talking
press pause
wait 0.5

# --- a thing with something written on it -----------------------------------------------
# The machines have bolted notices to their gates since worldgen was written.
# Until today not one of them could be read: use only ever offered what could be
# worked, and Takes has no row for a sign.
near sign
press use
await reading 4
wait 0.4
shot 04-a-notice-that-can-be-read with reading
press use
wait 0.4
shot 05-back-to-the-world with land:coast
